        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0303" n="294" xml:id="pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24 Raw Materials/954: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-20">May 20,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received May 20—4:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1278. The purport of the Department’s 876, May 16 and 886, May 17, regarding tin
                    has been informally conveyed to the Colonial Office which is looking into the
                    question. In the meantime it would like to know what is the amount of the
                    addition to American stocks which is desired and during what period of time, i.
                    e. both stocks of American tin consumers and the reserve stock in which the
                    Government would be involved. In this connection see the Embassy’s 1247 of May
                    17.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
